# Staged by fisher-4yn.1 on 2026-11-25 for a search that makes cutoffs.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# (go depth, info, bestmove and quit); fisher-4yn, "Nodes", grilled with the
# owner on 2026-11-24 (fisher-r6y D36 and D38, rule 7 of fisher-2aj);
# published perft in expectations/perft.epd (20 at depth 1, 400 at depth 2).
# Full info spelling: fisher-r6y D41 and Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), as cited
# in expectations/README.md. D28 makes nodes a total since the go.
#
# Derivation. A node is counted each time a move is played, including the
# reply that causes a cutoff; the root counts nothing (D38).
# Depth 1 plays the 20 root moves: 20 nodes, each scored cp 0 by material.
# Depth 2: every root move has 20 replies, and no capture is possible within
# two plies, so every position two plies in has material 0. The first root
# move costs 1 + 20 nodes and gives the root a score of cp 0. Each of the
# other 19 root moves costs 1 + 1, because its first reply already scores
# cp 0 for the side to move, which proves the root move no better than the
# first: a cutoff, and the remaining 19 replies are left unplayed. Depth 2
# enters 21 + 19 * 2 = 59 nodes. The count does not depend on the order of
# moves. The total since the go is 20 + 59 = 79.
# The score is cp 0 at both depths, as minimax gives (expectations/README.md).
#
# A search without cutoffs reports 440 (20 + 20 + 400) at depth 2, and so
# does one that cuts only on a reply strictly better than the bound, so
# neither passes this session.
> position startpos
> go depth 2
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 20 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp 0 nodes 79 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}

> quit
! exit
